## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design policy-grounded assistants with explainable outputs and integrated escalation.

## Key Concepts
- Grounding with Cognitive Search embeddings
- Confidence scoring and provenance tracking
- Safe escalation to ticketing (ServiceNow)
- Data lineage and logging for audits

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: compute final answer with grounding and provenance
async function answer(query) {
  const docs = await searchKB(query);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(query, docs);
  const res = await openai.complete({ prompt });
  const provenance = docs.map(d => d.id);
  const confidence = res.meta?.confidence ?? 0.9;
  if (confidence < 0.8) await ticketSystem.create('Review needed', { query, provenance });
  return { text: res.text, confidence, provenance };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle KB versioning and rollback?
- How would you validate calibration of confidence scores in production?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of cloud AI wiring, cost controls, and data safety in a beginner-friendly Azure setup.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI Service behind API Management
- Blob Storage for knowledge base
- Azure Cognitive Search for grounding
- PII redaction in input
- Per-tenant token-budget gate

## Code Example
```javascript
// Redaction example
function redactPII(text) {
  return text.replace(/\b\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}\b/g, "[REDACTED_DATE]");
}
```
```javascript
// Budget guard example
function withinBudget(nextTokens, budget, spent) {
  return spent + nextTokens < budget;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical implementation of policy-driven AI in multi-tenant analytics, including query rewriting, PII handling, budget-aware gating, KB grounding, and end-to-end auditing.

## Key Concepts

- Fine-grained access policies (RLS), prompt hygiene
- Query rewriting to enforce security
- Budget gating and cost controls
- KB grounding with Cognitive Search
- Auditing to Data Lake and PKI isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo function to rewrite a SQL prompt with tenant policy
function rewriteQuery(sql, policy) {
  // append where clause from policy
  const where = `(${policy.whereClause})`;
  return sql.replace(/WHERE/i, where);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test policy coverage and false positives?
- How would you scale policy updates without downtime?
